  {
   "evidence": "The statement's left-hand side is `(atlasEquiv hC\u2081 hC\u2081' h\u2081 h\u2081').trans (atlasEquiv hC\u2082 hC\u2082' h\u2082 h\u2082')` and its right-hand side is `atlasEquiv hC hC' (h\u2081.trans h\u2082) (h\u2082'.trans h\u2081')`. `hC` and `hC'` appear only on the right-hand side, and the file proves no `ReadsFrom` composition lemma that could supply them.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/VectorBundle/Sobolev/Atlas/ChartData.lean",
   "fix": "Remove `@[simp]` from the generic lemma, matching the unannotated generic `changeAtlas_changeAtlas` and `changeAtlas_comp`. Keep `@[simp]` on the `SobolevSection` and `BorderedSobolevSection` instances, where the `ReadsFrom` proofs are concrete terms (`readsFrom_sectionChartData` / `readsFrom_halfSectionChartData`).",
   "issue": "`@[simp] SectionChartData.atlasEquiv_trans` has `hC : C.ReadsFrom C'' \u03bc` and `hC' : C''.ReadsFrom C \u03bc` on its right-hand side but not on its left. Simp cannot instantiate them because `ReadsFrom` is an opaque `def` its discharger cannot prove, so the simp lemma practically never fires.",
   "line": 366
  }
